Lock screen fingerprint vs suspend: suspending while the lock screen scans cancels the
scan ("Cannot run while suspended"), which showed a red "FP ERROR:" (always with an empty
message) and could leave the reader dead until the next lock. Now the scan is paused on
PrepareForSleep and restarted 1.5s after resume, one-off errors retry silently, retries
never give up for good, and a reader that keeps failing gets a readable message. After
five errors in a row it retries every 35s rather than 5s: fprintd can be left unable to
reopen the reader after such a sleep, and it only restarts once it has had 30s without
requests (the root fix is fprint-sleep-install).
